---
const repo = 'https://github.com/CrashServer/webfoxdot-dev';
const shell = `# 1. Clone
git clone git@github.com:CrashServer/webfoxdot-dev.git webfoxDot
cd webfoxDot

# 2. Start the dev server (sets the COOP/COEP headers WASM needs)
python3 serve.py

# 3. Open http://127.0.0.1:8765 and click "boot"`;
---
<section id="start">
  <div class="wrap start-grid">
    <div class="start-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">./boot.sh</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Three commands, then it's your problem</h2>
      <p class="section-lead">
        The only hard requirement is Python 3 for the dev server — it sets the
        cross-origin isolation headers <code class="inline">SharedArrayBuffer</code>
        (and therefore scsynth) demands. Double-clicking
        <code class="inline">index.html</code> won't work, and yes, we all tried
        it first.
      </p>
      <ul class="start-list">
        <li><b>Python 3.8+</b> — for the dev server, that's it</li>
        <li><b>A browser from this decade</b> — Chrome 90+ / Firefox 90+</li>
        <li><b>SuperCollider</b> — only if you catch the synth-building bug</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="start-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Get the code ▸
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={`${repo}#readme`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Read the docs
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="start-note">
        Playing a gig? Any static host works — just send the
        <code class="inline">Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy</code> and
        <code class="inline">Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy</code> headers, or the
        browser silently confiscates your audio engine. Nginx, Apache and Caddy
        snippets are in the README.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="term">
      <div class="term-bar">
        <span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span>
        <span class="term-title">bash</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="term-body"><code>{shell}</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .start-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .start-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 26px 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .start-list li { padding-left: 22px; position: relative; }
  .start-list li::before {
    content: "▸";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--green);
  }
  .start-list b { color: var(--text-1); font-weight: 600; }
  .start-cta { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .start-note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-2); margin: 0; max-width: 56ch; }

  .term {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-2);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-1);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 60px -30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8);
  }
  .term-bar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    padding: 11px 14px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-1);
  }
  .dot { width: 11px; height: 11px; border-radius: 50%; }
  .dot.r { background: #f85149; }
  .dot.y { background: #d29922; }
  .dot.g { background: #3fb950; }
  .term-title {
    margin-left: 8px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--text-2);
  }
  .term-body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 20px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--text-1);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .start-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; } }
</style>
